  "title": "Peak Power Window",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "story": "The core logged N power readings. SIGMA needs the stretch of K readings in a row with the **biggest total**.\n\nInput: `N K` (1 ≤ K ≤ N ≤ 1000), then N whole numbers (each −10000 to 10000).\n\nOutput: `sum S at P`, where S is the biggest total of K consecutive readings and P is where that stretch starts (1 = the first reading). If several tie, use the earliest.\n\nExample: `5 2` then `1 9 3 7 5` prints `sum 12 at 2` (9 + 3).",
  "starter": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint readings[1000];\n\nint main(void) {\n    int n, k;\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &k);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &readings[i]);\n    }\n    // find the best window of k readings\n    return 0;\n}\n",
